{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>El. Tzapha.</b> It is the tzaphoni [adder] and it is more severe than the snake, and the meaning is that Hezekiah will be mightier than his father, and he will harm the Philistines, for thus it is written in Kings: he struck Gaza and its border from the watchtower of Naṣim to the fortified city (2 Kings 18:8)." "And the offspring it gives — <b>a flying seraph</b>, and the flying one is more severe among the seraphim."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:51.247358912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}